1
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:39,000
One Man, One Mission, One Choice

2
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Capsule is a drama, history, science fiction film directed by Andrew Martin.

3
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:45,000
1959: Guy is an experienced British fighter pilot who is in
command of Britain's first manned mission to space.

4
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:18,000
He has trained for this for three years at the height of the Cold War and now he is
alone in space, suffering Hypoxia, with a malfunctioning capsule.

5
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:51,000
He has limited contact with the UK, some unusual communication with the US and
some unorthodox communication with Tyuratam deep in Soviet Russia.

6
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Can he get home?

7
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Who will help him?

8
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Will he make the right choice?

9
00:40:57,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Guy Taylor, played by Edmund Kingsley.

10
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Charlotte Taylor, played by Lisa Greenwood.

11
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Harry Lyndhurst, played by David Wayman.

12
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Agent Mike Spann, played by Nigel Barber.

13
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:15,000
Graham Bennett, played by Gil Kolirin.

14
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:48,000
Bob Elijah, played by Michael Koltes.

15
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
A time capsule is a historic cache of goods or information, usually intended as a deliberate method of
communication with future people, and to help future archaeologists, anthropologists, or historians.

16
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
The preservation of holy relics dates back for millennia, but the practice of preparing and preserving a
collection of everyday artifacts and messages to the future appears to be a more recent practice.

17
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
Time capsules are sometimes created and buried during celebrations such as world's
fairs or cornerstone layings for buildings or at other ceremonies.

18
01:21:54,000 --> 01:22:00,000
The film explores themes of spacecraft, spy, deception, alone, space.

19
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:33,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
